<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria sells 10.42 bln levs 1-wk, 4-wk T-bills.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria sells 10.42 bln levs 1-wk, 4-wk T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry on Thursday sold two discount T-bill issues with maturities of one week and four weeks, yielding 3.75 percent and 17.61 percent to maturity, respectively, the central bank said.</p>
<p>Bids were received for a total of 10.468 billion levs of T-bills but the ministry approved bids for 10.418 billion levs.</p>
<p>Details of the issues follow:</p>
<p> Issue number		  BG3013097004	 BG3013197002</p>
<p> Term			    one week	     four weeks</p>
<p> Auction date		  January 30, 1997   January 30, 1997</p>
<p> Issue date		    January 30, 1997   January 30, 1997</p>
<p> Maturity date		 February 6, 1997   February 27, 1997</p>
<p> Bids received		 6,488 million levs     3,980 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	   96.39 pct	    85.03 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		 6,438 million levs     3,980 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	  96.39 pct	    85.03 pct</p>
<p> Avg yield to maturity     3.75 pct	     17.61 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
